roject  in the means of that they want to  take the project forward to a poster or  a publication  though that depends of course on the  complexity of your project  on the time that you are available to  give for that project but we typically  have  seen that our participants are able to  come up with a project even  high school students in very short  period of time which is like three  months  and for this program we typically  recommend  at least six to eight hours per week  to be able to come up with that project  so the program  starts with training and then we work  with you  by assigning you a mentor from our team  who works along with you in helping you  develop that project so you go through  an  intense training session and this  project  please note that is your own project we  do not offer you the topics or we do not  provide the topics  you are free to choose your own topic  what we do is provide you that  mentorship where you are able to  understand whether the project that you  have chosen  is going to have some reproducible  results  whether that project you can apply it in  different  places like for publication or if you  want to submit a paper for review  poster presentation so we work with you  uh through this and here are some of  these  examples right here of projects  so i'm also going to be sharing this  link in the chat box  for everybody  and you would see that these projects  are done  by a mixed group of people by mixed i  mean that  participants have come from high school  from research level  from undergraduate masters phd level so  this is really like for everybody  whoever is  interested in doing a project you can  actually go ahead and watch  these video sessions which are recorded  by the participants themselves where  they speak about their own project so  that you can learn about this entire  process  so i would leave you all to explore this  now the next program that we offer  and which is coming up right now after  this is  this program in collaboration with all  india institute of medical  sciences new delhi so we have this  workshop on lymphoma  and you can register for this program  by filling out the form at the bottom of  the page which i'm going to be coming to  next  then the other program which we  discussed briefly in today's session is  the omixlogic transcriptomics program so  this is also  part of the bioinformatics for  infectious disease program  that we have been discussing today so  this program is starting now on  april 16th and the registrations are  open to join this program right at the  moment  so you can go ahead and check this  program as well as you understand that  this program will have  transcriptomics for infectious disease  research and we also have  another program that is starting in  india with a lot of our collaborators  and this is on biomedical data science  and drug discovery so you can also join  this program  and so how do you join either of these  programs you have to fill only one form  and once you come down here you can  choose which  program you are interested in so you do  not have to fill multiple forms you can  choose  right here and even if you want to apply  for multiple programs uh consider  filling out the form twice  so that you are able to submit it twice  and you will receive  details regarding this in case any of  the details  are not very clear to you again  or you want to ask us more questions  please feel free to again reach out to  me marketing at pine.bio and i would be  able to clear those  out for you so abu curry has a question  here  i would like to address it at this  moment are the python coding  courses paid so the python coding  courses again some lessons are free  while some lessons  require a subscription so  if you can get the recording of the  session so i think daniel  uh yes we will be sharing the recording  of the session of course  so yeah so i think that i have answered  the question  now on regarding access to the tbio info  platform  so the programs that we have mentioned  here  all come with educational access to tbio  info which means that  whatever cost that you're paying for  each of these program covers the cost of  the tbio info license  but in case you are interested in just  exploring the tbio info  platform we also have  uh another licensing here which  makes it clear for you how to get  started  with getting access to the tbi info  platform it's called the gene lab  for researchers we offer a research  license where you're able to work with  your own data  at 99 per month but for first-time users  you have to  take this license for three months which  is 297.  so that is the research license while  the educational license which comes with  all of our programs costs 75 dollars per  month  while all of the programs already  include this in their pricing  so anybody who joins any of the  omixlogic training programs will have  access to tbio info the access would be  created by  us and sent to you so if you have any  questions regarding that as well  uh we would be able to help you with  this so  let us know if you have any questions  about this and i will be able to help  you  and while you are here i wanted to  welcome you to join us here  on linkedin and some of our other social  media networks so we have this group  in linkedin where we keep on sharing  many interesting posts  and not just posts we also keep sharing  job opportunities as well as  any other things which are relevant to  the bioinformatics community that we  have so please feel free  to go ahead and join this group we also  have a group  in facebook so please feel free to  follow us on facebook  as well and here is our instagram page  so we also keep on sharing all of these  updates  on instagram as well as do polls  sometimes on our story so  please go ahead and follow us there if  you are  more active on instagram and now again i  would like to go ahead and ask if you  have  any questions so that i may answer them  and  we can then take those questions so  thank you all again  and while we are going towards the end  what i wanted to mention here is that we  also  offer scholarships for our programs  that any participant can avail these  scholarships  are given to participants  with whom we have an interaction so the  process of the scholarship is this that  you fill out the form at the bottom of  this page  you need to mention your references from  your college or university  who go ahead and join that meeting with  us so any one of your references can  get on that meeting with us and once we  have spoken  to the reference and understood why you  would need that scholarship  uh you would be receiving all the  details from our end  so you can use utilize this option for  any of our programs that are here so  please feel free to  post them down and fill out that form  if you think that you require that  scholarship to join any of the programs  and i hope that  this was clear to everybody so again if  you have  any questions if you want to reach out  to us we have the email id marketing at  pine.bio  we have also shared dr mohit's email id  so you can also reach out to him  for any kind of research question that  you may have  so thank you all again for joining us  today  yeah thank you so much murray  okay it's wonderful to have you all here  we'll share the recording and all of the  links  to today's session via email with you  all  and have a lovely week ahead everybody  thank you again
 

